  "notes": "Source: AdventHealth University 2025-2026 Academic Catalog, 'Program: Biomedical Sciences, B.S.' (catalog.ahu.edu, catoid=74). Hand-transcribed 2026-09-30. TRIMESTER HOURS: AdventHealth University uses a trimester calendar; the catalog states degree totals in trimester hours (e.g., 'a minimum of 120 trimester hours'). All credit values here are trimester hours as stated. Catalog curriculum: Humanities 6 (choose from HMNT 310/314/325), Math 6 (MATH 120 + STAT 215, both mandatory), Religion 9 (RELP 103 mandatory + one of RELE 305/405 + one of RELP 243/RELT 368), Science 66 (60 mandatory + choose 6 from BIOL 350/402/410/410L), Electives 8 (any subject area), Total 120. The listed sections sum to 95; the remaining 25 credits are NOT itemized on the program page, so they are modeled as general-education elective choice slots distributed across trimesters (the per-trimester split is the collector's arrangement, disclosed). AHU's General Education policy requires BS students to complete 30 gen-ed credits with at least 3 in each of English & Composition, Social & Behavioral Sciences, Mathematics, Natural Sciences, and Religion & Humanities. The catalog gives no term-by-term sequence; trimester placement below is the collector's arrangement following science prerequisite chains (e.g., CHEM 151/152 before Organic I/II before Biochemistry), disclosed, not a catalog claim. For the 'choose 6' science electives: only pairs of the 3-credit courses (BIOL 350, 402, 410) can total 6; BIOL 410L (1 cr) is on the catalog's list but cannot by itself satisfy the 6-credit requirement. Completion requirements (not modeled as courses): minimum 120 trimester hours, 42 upper-division credits, 2.50 cumulative GPA, 60 hours in residence, 'C' or above in all required courses/electives, service-learning, competency assessment, MCAT prep for self-declared students.",
